# What the frozen workspace service is built from (final package review, item 09).
#
# The service's own dependencies, plus the freezer itself. Compiled to
# `sidecar-requirements.lock` with hashes, and installed into a clean
# environment by `scripts/build-sidecar.mjs` — so two people building the same
# commit install the same bytes, and a compromised or merely different version
# of a dependency cannot walk in through a developer's global site-packages.
#
#   python -m piptools compile --generate-hashes --strip-extras \
#     --output-file apps/desktop/sidecar-requirements.lock \
#     apps/desktop/sidecar-requirements.in
#
# The lock is resolved for the platform it is compiled on. This release is
# Windows x64 / CPython 3.13, which is what it therefore pins.

-r ../api/requirements.txt

# The freezer. Pinned here rather than taken from whatever a machine has,
# because it decides how the binary is laid out and what it carries.
pyinstaller>=6.11,<7
